## Open Defects — ACTIVE

### D1: Spill Backend Not Wired (P2, blocks Phase 12)
- Location: context_optimizer.rs, spill strategy
- Current: spill preserves content in-memory, records as "skipped" in trace
- Expected: spill writes to SpillBackend, returns SpillRef (20 tokens)
- Impact: spill strategy is a no-op in production (never actually frees tokens)
- Fix: implement SpillBackend trait + LocalFs impl (Phase 12.2)

### D2: EmergentContext Not Populated (P2, blocks Phase 11)
- Location: context_sources.rs, EmergentContext struct
- Current: EmergentContext always empty (no runtime writes to it)
- Expected: previous turn's discovered_skills, prefetched_memory fed in
- Impact: emergent tier never contributes to context (cold start every turn)
- Fix: wire agentic loop to populate from previous turn (Phase 11.1)

### D3: SessionLatches Struct Exists But Never Latched (P2, blocks Phase 11)
- Location: context_optimizer.rs, place_cache_markers()
- Current: latches parameter reserved but unused (always default values)
- Expected: first beta header evaluation latches value for session
- Impact: cache markers may be placed on unstable prefix (cache breaks)
- Fix: implement latch-on-first-use in runtime adapter (Phase 11.1)

### D4: PipelineStats Not Carried Across Turns (P1, blocks Phase 11)
- Location: context_pipeline.rs, PipelineStats
- Current: stats exist in tests but no runtime storage across turns
- Expected: stats accumulate within session, persisted across restarts
- Impact: every turn has cold pressure estimates (no learning)
- Fix: add PipelineStats to loop state (Phase 11.2), persist (Phase 12.1)

### D5: place_cache_markers() Latch-Aware Logic Not Implemented (P3)
- Location: context_optimizer.rs:~390
- Current: `latches` parameter passed but not used in marker placement
- Expected: suppress trailing markers if latch flip would invalidate prefix
- Impact: rare edge case — only triggers on mid-session config change
- Fix: implement conditional marker suppression (can defer to Phase 14)

### D6: allow_llm_summary Gate Has No Implementation (P3)
- Location: OptimizeLimits struct
- Current: `allow_llm_summary: true` field exists but no summarization logic
- Expected: LLM-based section summarization as compaction strategy
- Impact: one compaction strategy unavailable (others compensate)
- Fix: implement LLM summary strategy (requires async LLM call in optimizer)
- Note: may never implement — cost/latency tradeoff unclear

### D7: Cross-Agent Cache Sharing Limited to ForkPrefix (P3)
- Location: context_sources.rs, design doc §3.3
- Current: parent→child cache sharing via ForkPrefix (working)
- Expected: peer-to-peer sharing for same-skill agents
- Impact: missed cache opportunities in multi-agent scenarios
- Fix: design peer cache protocol (deferred — complex coordination problem)

## Known Limitations (by design, not defects)

### L1: No Information Density Tracking
- Pipeline allocates budget by tier/section, not by measured utility
- Would require LLM-as-judge to measure which sections influence responses
- Deferred to Phase 14.4 (stretch goal)

### L2: No Adaptive Breakpoint Placement
- Cache markers at fixed scope boundaries (Global→Session, Session→None)
- Optimal placement requires N turns of data + A/B testing
- Deferred to Phase 14.4 (stretch goal)

### L3: Predictive Pressure Uses Percentiles Not ML
- Response token estimates use percentile-based heuristic (p75/p95)
- Could train a model on (query_type, tool_count, history_length) → output_tokens
- Current approach is good enough (±20% accuracy) and zero latency

### L4: No Per-Provider Compaction Tuning
- Same compaction thresholds (0.60/0.75/0.90) for all providers
- Optimal thresholds differ (Anthropic cache is more sensitive than OpenAI)
- Could add per-provider tier boundaries to ProviderCachePolicy

### L5: Tool Result Clearing Is Coarse-Grained
- Clears entire tool_result content, not selective preservation
- Could keep first N lines or extract key facts before clearing
- Would require per-tool-type clearing strategies

